{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/424767-demon-vs-demon-stories","id":424767,"title":"Demon Vs. Demon Stories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T19:49:50-08:00","id":424767,"title":"Demon Vs. Demon Stories","content":"Does anyone have any advice or experience using other Demons, specifically, other Demon <i>agencies</i> as antagonists? I'm running a story with the players facing off against the Moscow Agency ( they of the human trafficking and forced soul-pacts) and trying to sabotage their most unsavory actions.<br /> <br /> My players have tangled with rogue demons as combat antagonists, but are there any specific concerns when groups of demons take covert action against one another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T22:08:14-08:00","id":424897,"title":"","content":"Yes. Demons will rewrite your family away into their family. They will make people you care about forget everything about you. They will dismantle your support network from inside by literally changing reality so that your support network ever existed. Then they will find some way to sic angels on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T22:14:19-08:00","id":424900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/424767-demon-vs-demon-stories?p=424897#post424897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Demons will rewrite your family away into their family.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026I'm sorry, I had to:<br /> <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/mikudemon.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Anyway, one of the big concerns when facing other demons that you don't directly get from, say, angels is the fact of aetheric resonance as a tool at the enemy's disposal, to say nothing of how the opposition can marshal specialized forces of occult physics on the fly at a much faster clip than the Machine usually manages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-02-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T22:37:01-08:00","id":424904,"title":"","content":"Slightly off-topic, sorta: given the \u201ctechgnostic espionage\u201d tagline for <b>Demon</b>, my mind immediately translated the subject line from \u201cDemon vs. Demon\u201d to \u201cSpy vs. Spy\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T05:26:45-08:00","id":425034,"title":"","content":"The most obvious Demon v Demon storyline is based on the Integrators. They tend to become compromised via angels. Actually, any demon can be compromised and sell out their fellows to the God Machine, but the Turncoats are renowned for it. <br /> <br /> With Sabatours, well, its an established fact that destroying some Infrastructure can have nasty effects. Like, oh, computers crashing world wide, or natural disasters. How much do you mind collateral damage? <br /> <br /> Tempters and Interogators are harder; I haven't quite figured something out for them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:09:25-08:00","id":425226,"title":"","content":"Demons are a nightmarish enemy in covert warfare. You don't know if anyone you're speaking to or looking at is Unchained, or one of their dupes. Take a good look at some of the Embeds and Exploits, like Stalking Horse, Demon House, Living Shadow and Living Recorder. Demons can find you. They can spy on you and you'll never know it. Are you paranoid yet?<br /> <br /> Remember that unless they use their supernatural powers (or they're actively glitching) demons are almost impossible to detect, since they can spoof active detection-powers and can lie flawlessly. If they have a few Cover options, they can cycle between them to keep you guessing. Are you paranoid yet?<br /> <br /> Murder By Improbability is useless against demons, but not against their allies. If they learn too much about you a wave of accidents is likely. They can achieve similar results with Embeds like Combustion. They can turn allies using powers like Imagine or Unperson.<br /> <br /> And, of course, gadgets make things even more complicated. One-shot gadgets with Hellfire built in are a terrifying supernatural firebomb, Bugs and listening devices are possible, and, my, has nobody ever considered using the Possession Exploit for a gadget?<br /> <br /> Pacts stealing bits and pieces of your life are a risk, sure, but they're not even top of the list. When demons are after you, absolute paranoia is a rule of thumb. Assume everyone and everything is a spy. Assume you're always being watched. Any object or situation is a potential trap. Assume your safehouses and allies are one step from being compromised, if they aren't already.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's how most demons feel all the time anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 03-02-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:20:59-08:00","id":425235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/424767-demon-vs-demon-stories?p=425034#post425034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tempters and Interogators are harder; I haven't quite figured something out for them yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tempters? Those self-serving bastards? Why, one of them might make a deal with an angel, selling you to save his own slimy skin! They'll ruin your life to extort Pacts and favors from you. They'll make you pay through the nose for their help when you're desperate and vulnerable. They'll snatch up every resource in the area and refuse to share, laughing at 'common causes' and 'greater goods'.<br /> <br /> And those bloody Inquisitors? They know everything,but they never <i>share</i> everything. They'll tell you where the Infrastructure is, sure, but they'll neglect to mention the angel guarding it - your horrible death is a chance for them to find out more information. They don't want to get their hands dirty. They want to play spymaster and will do everything they can to make you do their legwork. And they'll make you question everything you do, even turning against you when they think fighting the God-Machine is suddenly a bad idea. Cowards, to a man!<br /> <br /> And Saboteurs are worse than you think. Sure, they might blow up the Infrastructure that prevents a disaster, but they're more likely to blow up something that has no effect beyond pissing the God-Machine off. And when It is angry, when It sends hunter angels out of the hive to find the bastard throwing stones, other demons get stung. Saboteurs are at war. You're a potential, and very disposable, asset in their war. They might trick you into working for them, try to recruit you by siccing angels and cryptids on you, use you as a distraction while they attack their targets... There's a reason we call them Thugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 03-02-2015, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T06:28:00-08:00","id":426505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/424767-demon-vs-demon-stories?p=425235#post425235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tempters? Those self-serving bastards? Why, one of them might make a deal with an angel, selling you to save his own slimy skin! They'll ruin your life to extort Pacts and favors from you. They'll make you pay through the nose for their help when you're desperate and vulnerable. They'll snatch up every resource in the area and refuse to share, laughing at 'common causes' and 'greater goods'.<br /> <br /> And those bloody Inquisitors? They know everything,but they never <i>share</i> everything. They'll tell you where the Infrastructure is, sure, but they'll neglect to mention the angel guarding it - your horrible death is a chance for them to find out more information. They don't want to get their hands dirty. They want to play spymaster and will do everything they can to make you do their legwork. And they'll make you question everything you do, even turning against you when they think fighting the God-Machine is suddenly a bad idea. Cowards, to a man!</div> </div> </div> </div> Putting aside the sell-out-to-angels bit (which I associate more with the Turncoats), these are basically crying because other demons won't share their toys. Demons are hardly entitled to the fruits of other's labor. Its nothing more than than crying over sour grapes there. Not antagonist material.<br /> <br /> Turncoats actively sell out other demons. Sabatours actively cause havoc and kill and destroy things. These are both actions that actively interfere with another. Crying that a Tempter won't give you something out of the goodness of its heart? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:25:56-08:00","id":426561,"title":"","content":"I was kinda writing those in character. I think it's still worth mentioning,though. A demon withholding what you desperately need and hoarding resources can be an antagonist. They're not killing you, they're just making your life difficult and you hate dealing with them but you don't have a choice. That's an antagonist to me, that's a crimelord who eventually demons might decide is hurting the cause so much they may as well be working for the enemy (especially to hardline Saboteurs). It's an archetype that crops up in a lot of Requiem games.<br /> <br /> You can take it further, if that isn't antagonist-y enough for you. Have a Tempter who will kill you for your gadgets, your suborned Infrastructure and human allies/assets you've accrued (it's not hard to take control of a cult if the original demonic patron is gone). You don't get to reign in hell unless you're prepared to hurt a few other devils.<br /> <br /> As for Inquisitors using you as guinea pigs, I think that flat-out counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 03-03-2015, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:41:34-08:00","id":426756,"title":"","content":"Dealing with other Demons is like the Machine, in a way, because your only protection is your cover. Any sane Demon is going to have a specific cover it uses to interact with any given agency. If things get sticky, they can burn the cover and move on. This is the only way you can be 'sure' other Demons can't leverage and develop you as an asset, though it's somewhat less likely they will try than one might initially assume. Demons make unappealing assets, despite the many talents they have.<br /> <br /> The reason why? Developing demonic assets is not easy. Unlike humans, Demons are manifest ideologies... that thing with them taking strange, often alien virtues is very significant when considered in the context of intelligence work. Demons are motivated by an often completely cryptic (to you) ideology. If you leverage a demon by stealing his fake daughter, he might cry and seem to feel genuinely distraught, but his actual motivation might simply be to develop more advanced musical compositions or to fully understand the color blue or any number of other insane psychological configurations that normal humans just don't have.<br /> <br /> This is what makes intelligence work with other demons particularly difficult. In espionage, you always want to be able to control your asset, to force them in some way to do what you need them to do because you can count on the basic human response to blackmail, violence, shame or other jeopardy. Other Demons aren't so easily quantified. They only fake being distressed like humans do, most of the time. And if things ever get really bad, they simply move on to other lives.<br /> <br /> I propose that most Demons interacting with other Demons assume the cover they are currently interacting with is not particularly valuable. If they see obvious routes of attack, they probably think twice before exploiting them. They're dealing with fake people, after all. What seems like weakness is probably strength. The daughter in the previous example is TOO tempting a target. Why did he approach us in a cover with easily located family? Is this a honeypot? Treachery and betrayal are common with such anonymity built into the system. The person who sold you out yesterday can come to you again tomorrow and you'll never know.<br /> <br /> At some point, Demons stop looking or caring whether the Cover they are dealing with is That Guy. They all just assume the worst, and all parties involved understand they MUST assume the worst. And every party in the negotiation understands this ; every time you speak to a Demon in a negotiation he mustt suspect (wisely) that you are in fact one of his most bitter enemies returned in a new face. You need to earn trust starting from that position.<br /> <br /> This creates an environment of ruthless pragmatism, frequent 'burned' covers that are not burned to the God Machine but nonetheless useless for practical purposes because people like Moscow want them dead, and intricate intelligence gambits between agencies. While demons are exceptionally potent as operatives the flip side of this is that they are 'too good' - they are nearly impossible to pin down, leverage or turn. While the insane ability of a Demon brings casts a long shadow over any informed discussion between agencies, that same power is so impossible to control or even locate that most Agencies tend to look at subordinates or employees before working on targeting actual Demons as intelligence assets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T10:14:58-07:00","id":434184,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that Demons are in a pretty fragile situation to begin with, and I'd guess that most accumulate valuable things they'd hate to part with. For an Inquisitor, it might be an occult library, for an Integrator, a piece of Suborned Infrastructure that makes him feel good; for a Tempter, that one restaurant that makes Coq au Vin just right, or that special boy/girl, or a favorite night club. Even dedicated Saboteurs need comrades and places to keep their stuff. And even from the viewpoint of ruthless pragmatism, it doesn't make sense to blow up mutually beneficial ongoing relationships for a one-time gain... unless that gain is really big. <br /> <br /> At the same time, Demons are universally good at ruining stuff and getting in trouble and can always bring down the heat on themselves or their enemies. So I would imagine a wary businesslike attitude is more common than the desire to harm others or get revenge. Even if you're pretty sure a colleague screwed you over on a deal, it's better to accept his since denial and take steps to protect yourself than to declare war. This also serves the purposes of genre emulation -- even James Bond spends most of each movie sniffing around the villain's operations before the big action scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4832-dannyk","name":"DannyK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:10:33-07:00","id":438227,"title":"","content":"All Unchained are amoral scumbags by nature, it's only an individual Demon's actions and goals that brings them closer to the humans they pretend to be.<br /> <br /> Unlike all other gameline monsters (with the exception of Prometheans) the Unchained were they never truly human and their defection to the human race is always one driven by very self-centered reasons (note that this doesn't mean that their Fall was wrong or ill-spirited, just that even those who Fall for love or to protect someone they care about still Fall due to very personal reasons.) That pared with their lingering Angelic tendancies (I.E. goal driven activities to further their own personal agenda/vision for the future) and machine like detatchment (Demon's can feel the full spectrum of human emotions, but don't necessarily have to base their desisions and actons around them like a normal human) can potentially lead to any Demon turning against their fellows. Consider the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Resources: The Unchained only have access to the resources that they can either acquire or take from the world around them, and these resources are not infinite. Imagine what would happen when two Rings or Agencies discover that they are both targeting the same buisness or individual to bolter their own armament against the God Machine and it's agents. How often would the two come together in mutual agreement? And even if they did could they really trust eachother?<br /> <br /> 2. Goals: Each Unchained has their own vision of Hell and what needs to be done to acquire/achieve it. Even Demon's who share Agendas can have very very very different views on how to get the job done and it's quite common for these conflicts of opinion to spill over into actual conflicts. For instance if one Saboteur believes that the key to taking down the Machine lies in the strategic destruction of Infrastructure while another firmly believe it involves freeing humanity from the Machine's influence then imagine what the latter would do when the former plans to detonate a bomb in the heart of Infastructure hidden beneath a suburban neighborhod.<br /> <br /> 3. Self Preservation: Honestly it's always better them than you. If an Agency accidently get's on the Machine's radar and they can easily shift the heat onto your own Ring then what's stopping them? Sure if your Ring survives there will be inevitable reprecussions but by that time the Agency in question will be waaaaay out of Dogde.<br /> <br /> 4. Personal Reasons: Speaking of reprecussions who holds a grudge better than any other monster in the World of Darkness? This can range from anything from a rival Demon turing someone your character cares about into Cover, making a Cover family member Stigmatic and having them now pose a threat to your Cover, pissing off the wrong people to the point where a bounty is placed upon one of your Chronicle's players, ect. Anything under the sun could work, and since Demons can be increadably long lived these grudges can be so old that the player characters might not even know that they'd incured such a wrath. After all Demons still feel human emotions but can react to them with the cold calculating logic of a machine.<br /> <br /> I cannot highly stress enough that while an Agenda can greatly impact a Demon's actions an Agenda itself is a philosophy that each individual Demon adheres to regarding how they structure their lives and goals. It may be tempting to just make them all Integrators, but unless you specifically want to examine what an Agency of Intigrators would be like I highly suggest that you utilize the full spectrum of Demon antagonists. Nothing would make your players question their actions more than to go up againts another Demon who's litterally willing to burn their brethern down around them if it means they can escape from the God Machine forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Fully Fleshing Out 03-12-2015, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:45:54-07:00","id":438332,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNo